WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.139 --> 00:00:05.900
In this section, we will continue exploring how version control is handled in the engine

2
00:00:05.900 --> 00:00:11.419
by seeing how it is managed in Unreal Engine for Fortnite, or UEFN.

3
00:00:11.419 --> 00:00:16.300
Now after launching UEFN, new users will be prompted to select or create a project

4
00:00:16.300 --> 00:00:18.039
from the project browser.

5
00:00:18.039 --> 00:00:22.120
Within the project browser, you will need to enable Unreal Revision Control to utilize

6
00:00:22.120 --> 00:00:27.620
the integrated version control tools available for your team inside UEFN.

7
00:00:27.620 --> 00:00:32.700
When first creating your project, UEFN Revision Control allows users the option of selecting

8
00:00:32.700 --> 00:00:37.859
a pre-existing team for each project that has been created and assigned by the project

9
00:00:37.859 --> 00:00:40.329
manager in the Creator Portal.

10
00:00:40.329 --> 00:00:44.429
If a pre-existing team hasn't been created for collaborative work, simply click on the

11
00:00:44.429 --> 00:00:50.950
Create a Team hyperlink inside the project browser under the Project Defaults for UEFN.

12
00:00:50.950 --> 00:00:54.850
This will take you directly to the Creator Portal to create or manage your team for

13
00:00:54.850 --> 00:00:56.469
this project.

14
00:00:56.469 --> 00:01:00.950
Here you can use the web-based Creator Portal to select your members, assign a team

15
00:01:00.950 --> 00:01:06.599
name, team description, and select projects to transfer to the newly created team.

16
00:01:06.599 --> 00:01:11.040
Once your project is launched, the Unreal Revision Control tools can be accessed through

17
00:01:11.040 --> 00:01:16.530
the main menu in UEFN, just like they are in Unreal Engine.

18
00:01:16.530 --> 00:01:20.629
Navigate up to the Tools pulldown in the main menu and move on down to the Revision

19
00:01:20.629 --> 00:01:22.599
Controls section.

20
00:01:22.599 --> 00:01:26.599
Version Control can also be accessed through the Revision Control Quick Access menu in

21
00:01:26.640 --> 00:01:31.200
the bottom right-hand corner of any window, just like Unreal Engine.

22
00:01:31.200 --> 00:01:35.359
Revision Control settings can be changed, set, or disabled by launching the Revision

23
00:01:35.359 --> 00:01:42.000
Control login menu from either access option, and UEFN does support Perforce as a Revision

24
00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:47.000
Control provider option if you don't want to use Unreal Revision Control.

25
00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:52.280
Here, just as you would in Unreal Engine, users will populate the server, username,

26
00:01:52.280 --> 00:01:55.260
and workspace where the project is located.

27
00:01:55.260 --> 00:01:59.739
Be aware that Unreal Engine for Fortnite is still considered in its beta, and support

28
00:01:59.739 --> 00:02:04.290
for Revision Control options will improve in future versions.

29
00:02:04.290 --> 00:02:05.709
That's all for this section.

30
00:02:05.709 --> 00:02:08.810
In our next section, we will take a look at Unreal GameSync.
